# --- appended by this fork -------------------------------------------------
#
# Everything above is upstream's own `.gitignore`, byte for byte: upstream's
# `src/.gitignore` is a second, separate file and is not merged into this one.
# Nothing above is removed to make room.
#
# The Zig package build writes its caches and its installation tree beside the
# sources. `src/.gitignore` already covers upstream's generated inputs
# (`luajit.h`, `lj_bcdef.h`, `lj_vm.S` and the rest), and this build writes those
# into the build cache rather than into `src/`, so the entries above are
# unchanged in meaning.
#
# No upstream entry is broad enough to swallow a file this fork adds, so nothing
# has to be re-included: the fork's own paths are `build.zig`, `build.zig.zon`,
# `build_support/`, `zig/`, `consumer/`, `tests.zig`, `smoke.zig` and `*.md`, and
# `*.lib` above matches `libunibreak`-style directories but not any of them.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/
zig-pkg/

# `consumer/` is a package in its own right, and running its own `zig build`
# inside this repository -- which is what CI's consumer step does -- would leave
# both directories inside it. They are listed here rather than excluded in
# `build.zig.zon`, because the manifest lists the consumer's three files by name
# for the same reason.
consumer/.zig-cache/
consumer/zig-out/